  "verbalization": "Borapetoside D is shown to have a target relationship with Hepatocyte and HaCaT, both of which are targets of compounds with a complex molecular structure involving spiro[4.5]decan-7-ylidene groups. These compounds are implicated in targeting Phosphodiesterase 6C, a key enzyme involved in the breakdown of cyclic nucleotides, which plays a role in cellular signaling and homeostasis. The evidence suggests that Borapetoside D may interact with cellular targets that ultimately lead to the inhibition of Phosphodiesterase 6C, potentially modulating intracellular signaling pathways. The scores from the different paths indicate a consistent level of confidence in the relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The observed targeting of Hepatocyte and HaCaT, which are distinct cell types, suggests that Borapetoside D may exert its effects through a broad cellular mechanism, possibly involving receptor-mediated pathways or enzyme inhibition.",
